"Fair splittings by independent sets in sparse graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.03268)\nciteturn5academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.2 years ago; Title: Fair splittings by independent sets in sparse graphs ... Given a partition $V_1 \\sqcup V_2 \\sqcup \\dots \\sqcup V_m$ of the vertex set of a graph, we are interested in finding multiple disjoint independent sets that contain the correct fraction of vertices of each $V_j$.\nTitle: Fair splittings by independent sets in sparse graphs\nAuthors: Alexander Black, Umur Cetin, Florian Frick, Alexander Pacun, Linus Setiabrata\nDate: Mon Sep 10 12:28:28 2018\n\nGiven a partition $V_1 \\sqcup V_2 \\sqcup \\dots \\sqcup V_m$ of the vertex set of a graph, we are interested in finding multiple disjoint independent sets that contain the correct fraction of vertices of each $V_j$. We give conditions for the existence of $q$ such independent sets in terms of the topology of the independence complex. We relate this question to the existence of $q$-fold points of coincidence for any continuous map from the independence complex to Euclidean space of a certain dimension, and to the existence of equivariant maps from the $q$-fold deleted join of the independence complex to a certain representation sphere of the symmetric group. As a corollary we derive the existence of $q$ pairwise disjoint independent sets accurately representing the $V_j$ in certain sparse graphs for $q$ a power of a prime.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFair splittings by independent sets in sparse graphs - arXiv Combinatorics (https://www.arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/1809.03268v1)\nciteturn5search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.2 years ago; Crawled: last month; ## Fair splittings by independent sets in sparse graphs ... Given a partition $V_1 \\sqcup V_2 \\sqcup \\dots \\sqcup V_m$ of the vertex set of a graph, we are interested in finding multiple disjoint independent sets that contain the correct fraction of vertices of each $V_j$.\n\n## Fair splittings by independent sets in sparse graphs\n\nAlexander Black, Umur Cetin, Florian Frick, Alexander Pacun, Linus Setiabrata\n\nPublished: 2018-09-10\n\nComments: 14 pages\n\nNote:\n\nJournal: Israel J. Math. 236, 603-627 (2020)\n\nDOI: 10.1007/s11856-020-1980-5\n\nequivariant euclidean space graph group symmetric group partition representation\n\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\n### Abstract\n\nGiven a partition $V_1 \\sqcup V_2 \\sqcup \\dots \\sqcup V_m$ of the vertex set of a graph, we are interested in finding multiple disjoint independent sets that contain the correct fraction of vertices of each $V_j$. We give conditions for the existence of $q$ such independent sets in terms of the topology of the independence complex. We relate this question to the existence of $q$-fold points of coincidence for any continuous map from the independence complex to Euclidean space of a certain dimension, and to the existence of equivariant maps from the $q$-fold deleted join of the independence complex to a certain representation sphere of the symmetric group. As a corollary we derive the existence of $q$ pairwise disjoint independent sets accurately representing the $V_j$ in certain sparse graphs for $q$ a power of a prime.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFair splittings by independent sets in sparse graphs (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/339211696_Fair_splittings_by_independent_sets_in_sparse_graphs)\nciteturn5search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; A similar theorem was shown for paths by Black et al. [9]: if G is a path and every set V i contains an odd number of points, then there exist two independent sets S 1 and S 2 , covering all but at most n vertices of G such that for every i \\in [n] it holds that ... ... As a result, we obtain constant inapproximability results for all known natural PPA-complete problems, including Necklace-Splitting, the Discrete-Ham-Sandwich problem, two variants of the pizza sharing problem, and for finding fair independent sets in cycles and paths. ... We show that this is true when H is the set of independent sets in a path, and conjecture that it is true when H is the set of matchings in $K_{n,n}$.\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nFair representation by independent sets\n\nArticle\n\n  * Nov 2016\n\n  * Ron Aharoni\n  * Noga Alon\n  * Eli Berger\n  * Ran Ziv\n\nFor a hypergraph H let $\\beta(H)$ denote the minimal number of edges from H covering V(H). An edge S of H is said to represent {\\em fairly} (resp. {\\em almost fairly}) a partition $(V_1,V_2, \\ldots, V_m)$ of V(H) if $|S\\cap V_i|\\ge \\lfloor\\frac{|V_i|}{\\beta(H)}\\rfloor$ (resp. $|S\\cap V_i|\\ge \\lfloor\\frac{|V_i|}{\\beta(H)}\\rfloor-1$) for all $i \\le m$. In matroids any partition of V(H) can be represented fairly by some independent set. We look for classes of hypergraphs H in which any partition of V(H) can be represented almost fairly by some edge. We show that this is true when H is the set of independent sets in a path, and conjecture that it is true when H is the set of matchings in $K_{n,n}$. We prove that partitions of $E(K_{n,n})$ into three sets can be represented almost fairly. The methods of proofs are topological.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNOVEL STRUCTURES IN STANLEY SEQUENCES (https://webpages.leeu.edu/rmoy/files/2018/08/novelstructure.pdf)\nciteturn5search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; While independent Stanley sequences are modular, the cardinality of their modular set ... modular p-Stanley sequences.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nF L O R I A N F R I C K (https://www.math.cmu.edu/users/math/ffrick/CV_short.pdf)\nciteturn5search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Fair splittings by independent sets in sparse graphs ... On the generalized Erd˝os–Kneser conjecture: Proofs and reducti